[all_together_subsections] parent=Experiments sample=3 attempt=1/3
1. AppxLP achieves a precision score of nearly 0.85 after reading only a single record.
2. AppxIPF and TANE initially perform as good as AppxLP but eventually drop to approximately 0.7 precision at 10%.
3. Pyro++ has the least precision throughout.
4. AppxLP outperforms all baselines after reading only 10% of the data and achieving a precision and NDCG score of 1 on the Student dataset.
5. ExLP and ExDCS are able to outperform approximate approaches after reading 40% data with a precision of 1.0.
6. AppxLP is around 7.49% faster than AppxIPF for error threshold = 3, 5.75% for error threshold = 5, and 10.74% for error threshold = 7.
